p.src:
At once, however, Zhang makes a practical refinement that is crucial. Although the framework is named in the order $3,2,1$, one need not enter it from the first slot. One may begin where the mind can get traction most quickly: $\text{entry}(F_{321}(T))
\in
\left\{
\text{1 thing about }T,\;
\text{2 types/ways of }T,\;
\text{3 steps for }T
\right\}.$ This is why the framework is usable under pressure. It is not a rigid script. It is a small menu of admissible decompositions.

